{"type":"standard","title":"David Jolly","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">David Jolly</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q15963996","titles":{"canonical":"David_Jolly","normalized":"David Jolly","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">David Jolly</span></span>"},"pageid":41148509,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/David_Jolly_%283x4%29.jpg/330px-David_Jolly_%283x4%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":440},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/66/David_Jolly_%283x4%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":480,"height":640},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1376320361","tid":"0cc718e0-b74b-11f1-9bec-cb56ab038e02","timestamp":"2026-09-23T12:33:59Z","description":"American attorney and politician (born 1972)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Jolly","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Jolly?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Jolly?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:David_Jolly"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Jolly","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/David_Jolly","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Jolly?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:David_Jolly"}},"extract":"David Wilson Jolly is an American politician who served as the U.S. representative for Florida's 13th congressional district from 2014 to 2017 as a Republican. After leaving office, Jolly became a prominent Republican critic of President Donald Trump and a political pundit. In September 2018, Jolly left the Republican Party.","extract_html":"<p><b>David Wilson Jolly</b> is an American politician who served as the U.S. representative for Florida's 13th congressional district from 2014 to 2017 as a Republican. After leaving office, Jolly became a prominent Republican critic of President Donald Trump and a political pundit. In September 2018, Jolly left the Republican Party.</p>"}